From 0c636fb6e6e8e439266da9aac49f0170ca546623 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robin Lintermann <rl@karo-electronics.de>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:29:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/imx/dpu95: don't spam error log when bridge attach defers
 probe

When no display is connected over DSI, the downstream bridge chain
(tc358762, panel) keeps returning -EPROBE_DEFER, so the DPU driver
probe is deferred and retried by the driver core on every subsequent
device probe. Each retry printed a KERN_ERR 'failed to attach bridge
to encoder for stream0: -517', spamming the console.

Treat -EPROBE_DEFER as a normal 'not ready yet' condition and log it
at debug level only, matching how drm_bridge.c itself handles it via
dev_err_probe(). Real errors are still reported with drm_err(). The
error code still propagates, so probe deferral behavior is unchanged
and a display connected at boot still brings the chain up.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Generated by Mistral Vibe.
Co-Authored-By: Mistral Vibe <vibe@mistral.ai>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-kms.c | 11 ++++++++---
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-kms.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-kms.c
index 4d298efc29c8..cdf66cec0721 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-kms.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/imx/dpu95/dpu95-kms.c
@@ -706,9 +706,14 @@ static int dpu95_kms_init_encoder_per_crtc(struct dpu95_drm_device *dpu_drm,
 	ret = drm_bridge_attach(encoder, bridge, NULL,
 				DRM_BRIDGE_ATTACH_NO_CONNECTOR);
 	if (ret) {
-		drm_err(drm,
-			"failed to attach bridge to encoder for stream%u: %d\n",
-			dpu_crtc->stream_id, ret);
+		if (ret == -EPROBE_DEFER)
+			drm_dbg_kms(drm,
+				    "bridge for stream%u not ready yet, deferring probe: %d\n",
+				    dpu_crtc->stream_id, ret);
+		else
+			drm_err(drm,
+				"failed to attach bridge to encoder for stream%u: %d\n",
+				dpu_crtc->stream_id, ret);
 		goto out;
 	}
 
